<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><b><i>&#160;</i></b></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 0.25in; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><b><i>The
Cayman Islands and the BVI</i></b></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 0.25in; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
Company was incorporated in the Cayman Islands and several of its wholly-owned subsidiaries were incorporated in the BVI. Under the current
laws of the Cayman Islands and the BVI, these entities are not subject to income or capital gains taxes. In addition, dividend payments
are not subject to withholding tax in the Cayman Islands and the BVI.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><b><i>&#160;</i></b></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 0.25in; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><b><i>Hong
Kong</i></b></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 0.25in; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">According
to the Tax (Amendment) (No. 3) Ordinance 2018 published by the Hong Kong government, effective April 1, 2018, under the two-tiered profits
tax regime, the profits tax rate for the first HKD<ix:nonFraction contextRef="c0" decimals="-6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:IncomeTaxReconciliationChangeInEnactedTaxRate" scale="6" unitRef="hkd" id="ixv-34832">2</ix:nonFraction> million of assessable profits is <ix:nonFraction contextRef="c215" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:EffectiveIncomeTaxRateReconciliationChangeInEnactedTaxRate" scale="-2" unitRef="pure" id="ixv-34833">8.25</ix:nonFraction>% (half of the rate specified in Schedule 8
to the Inland Revenue Ordinance (&#8220;IRO&#8221;)) for corporations. The Group was not subject to Hong Kong profits tax for any of
the periods presented as it did not have assessable profits during such periods.</span></p></ix:nonNumeric><div>

